    "before_row": "| 710 | 30003703 / OWR-15987-013 | Equality of the Andreadakis and Representation-Ring Filtrations | 0.1045 | 6.0 | 3 | 2018 | queued | 0/5 |  |  |  |",
    "after_row": "| 710 | 30003703 / OWR-15987-013 | Equality of the Andreadakis and Representation-Ring Filtrations | 0.1045 | 6.0 | 3 | 2018 | claimed_solved | 1/5 |  | Accepted explicit counterexamples to Satoh's 2018 component-filtration equality: D_n(5) != A_n(5) for every n >= 4; D_n(6) != A_n(6) for every n >= 3. Rational SL(2) matrix-entry algebra; integral free-group lower central series; D acts on the whole J quotient. Classical Burde and Razmyslov identity credit retained; no new PI identity or general PI method claimed. No degree-5 rank-3, every-degree, higher-SL_m, character-algebra or ordinary IA lower-central claim. Bounded priority audit retains 2017/2021 journal and 2025/2026 related-journal access limits; no historical firstness or current-openness certificate. Extensively AI-assisted, unrefereed preprint 10.5281/zenodo.23387442; internal AI review is not human peer review. [Original proof and audit](attempts/30003703/README.md); [published note and current priority status](publications/30003703/PUBLICATION.md). |  |",
